🚽 Test case: regression for #206 (3a) code review -- StructField dropped
🚽 modifiers entirely (no field to hold them), so a field reached through
🚽 a `lit giga`/`lit thicc` alias silently sized/aligned as a plain 4-byte
🚽 int instead of an 8-byte long/long long. get_struct_field_size() and
🚽 get_struct_field_alignment() (ast.c) now both read f->modifiers.
lit giga rizz Meters;

gang Distance {
    yap unit;    🚽 char,        1 byte, align 1 -> offset 0
    Meters value; 🚽 long (giga), 8 bytes, align 8 -> offset 8 (7 bytes padding)
};              🚽 total: 16, not 5 (1 + 4, if Meters were misread as int)

skibidi main {
    gang Distance d;
    yapping("%lu", maxxing(d));
}
